# Appointment API contract (backend only; no automatic appointment booking or push worker).
# Authorization: Bearer patient token on /me, doctor token on /doctor.
# A doctor can read/write ONLY appointments explicitly linked to that doctorId.
# Patient creation may nominate an active doctor; bookingStatus is then requested,
# never confirmed. No doctor creation on behalf of arbitrary patients is exposed.
# External doctor appointments have doctorId=null and bookingStatus=recorded.
# doctorName is a display snapshot entered by the patient, not a verified credential.
# Prescription issuer identity is the authenticated doctorId, never a request field.
# Appointment dates include offsets; timezone is an IANA name. Responses use UTC.
# State: scheduled -> cancelled/completed/no_show (no automatic attendance inference).
# Terminal states cannot be reopened; create a linked follow-up instead.
# Archive is reversible and independent of attendance state; no DELETE endpoint.
# Archived records are read-only except unarchive and doctor prescription revocation.
# Reminder preferences are stored only. The app must cancel reminders on archive or
# terminal state and must not reschedule expired reminder times for immediate firing.
# Lists default to all records, including archived, for offline reconciliation.
# List pagination orders by (userId,id), uses opaque nextCursor, max limit=100.
# Details include all notes/recipes and the 100 latest audit events.
# Save is a full replacement of editable fields, not PATCH. Defaults apply.
# Mutations require expectedVersion (0 for creation) and stable operationId.
# Retry the EXACT same operation after an uncertain network result. A 409 means
# fetch current state and resolve the conflict; do not auto-overwrite or regenerate IDs.
# Every successful action increments the appointment version. Prescription contents
# are immutable; replacement revokes the prior record and retains both originals.
# Patient notes and doctor-authored clinical notes are separate.
# Medication creation/inventory are NOT changed by issuing a prescription.
# App integration, reminder delivery, patient acceptance of treatment imports,
# and legal/electronic-signature workflows are outside this backend change.

@base = http://localhost:3000
@token = REPLACE_WITH_PATIENT_TOKEN
@doctorToken = REPLACE_WITH_LINKED_DOCTOR_TOKEN
@patientId = REPLACE_WITH_PATIENT_ID

### List own records. Continue with ?cursor=<nextCursor> when non-null.
GET {{base}}/appointments/me?limit=50&archived=all
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create (keep the same IDs across retries; examples are not executed automatically).
POST {{base}}/appointments/me/operations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "operationId": "appointment-create-example",
  "action": {
    "type": "save", "id": "appointment-example", "expectedVersion": 0,
    "appointment": {
      "doctorId": null, "doctorName": "Doctor externo", "specialty": "Medicina general",
      "start": "2026-11-05T10:00:00-06:00", "end": "2026-11-05T10:30:00-06:00",
      "timezone": "America/Mexico_City", "modality": "in_person",
      "location": "Consultorio", "address": "Dirección del consultorio",
      "mapUrl": null, "consultationUrl": null, "reason": "Revisión",
      "preparation": "Llevar estudios", "patientNotes": "",
      "followUpAt": null, "previousAppointmentId": null,
      "reminder24h": true, "reminder1h": true
    }
  }
}

### Load by ID (also supports opening a reminder without passing an app object).
GET {{base}}/appointments/me/appointment-example
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Patient operations: save, reschedule, status, archive, patient_notes.
# status includes status and reason; archive includes archived:true/false.
# patient_notes includes text and followUpAt (ISO date or null).
# reschedule includes start,end,timezone,reason and resets doctor confirmation.
# On save, doctorId and previousAppointmentId cannot change after creation.

### Doctor operations: confirm, reschedule, status, clinical_note,
# issue_prescription, revoke_prescription. All target an existing linked appointment.
# clinical_note: noteId,text. Only after confirmed consultation start.
# issue_prescription: prescriptionId,instructions,items,supersedesId(optional).
# Each item: id,name,ingredients,strength,form,dose,route,frequency,duration,
# instructions,asNeeded,maxDailyDose. Prescription quantities are authored text,
# never interpreted as stock or automatically converted into a treatment.
# revoke_prescription: prescriptionId,reason. Allowed even after archiving.
GET {{base}}/appointments/doctor?limit=50
Authorization: Bearer {{doctorToken}}

### Doctor detail
GET {{base}}/appointments/doctor/{{patientId}}/appointment-example
Authorization: Bearer {{doctorToken}}

### Confirmation example; patient must first link this doctor's ID on creation.
POST {{base}}/appointments/doctor/{{patientId}}/operations
Authorization: Bearer {{doctorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "operationId": "appointment-confirm-example",
  "action": { "type": "confirm", "id": "appointment-example", "expectedVersion": 1 }
}
